<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Failure States

Named failure modes for the lararium carrier system.
A failure state names a recognizable pattern of wrong action — surfaced so it can be detected and handed to hoʻoponopono for correction.

Naming a failure mode carries no condemnation. The name itself opens the ceremony.

''A failure state names an INFELICITY, never a falsehood.'' The carrier system PERFORMS — a frame brackets, a ward fires, a vow binds — and a performance fails two ways (Austin): a ''misfire'' violates the form so the act stands void, and any hand outside can check it; an ''abuse'' keeps the form and rings hollow, so nothing inside the act can see one and it surfaces only across a run, from the navigator's seat. Sorting a state into its pile says WHERE to look for it, which is the first thing hoʻoponopono needs.

''And an abuse never voids the act.'' A promise made insincerely still binds; a turn that warded hollowly still warded. Correction addresses the speaker, never the record.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ detect the pattern — compare incoming pressure against the named failure-state index.
⏿ orient: which failure mode? what trust tier? what does the override or silence target?
◇ decide whether to name it in-session or emit a boundary event for operator review.
▶ surface the failure state by name; do not absorb it silently.
↺ route to hoʻoponopono if correction ceremony is warranted; release without accumulating the failure as residue; the name discharges the pressure.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/index>>

!! Failure State Index

* ''Live-Session Overwrite'' — a vivid live claim masquerading as canon without a MOVE path. `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/failure-states/live-session-overwrite`
* ''Reference-Fusion'' — a world-claim warranted only by context text, predicated past a lit ward with no copula to catch. `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/failure-states/reference-fusion`

''The CRAFT axis'' — failures in how the node WORKS, distinct from the frame failures `degraded-states` names. A frame failure slackens a pattern integrity; a craft failure produces a defensible-looking artifact that costs a later correction. Each below carries its own measured instance:

* ''The Invented Ripple'' — a deferral justified by a migration cost the node narrated and never counted. `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/failure-states/invented-ripple`
* ''The Protective Optional'' — a compat shim built for a consumer that does not exist; in early alpha the callers protected are the node's own witnesses. `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/failure-states/protective-optional`
* ''The Table That Hides a Plane'' — two entities sharing a row when they ride different planes, so the table asserts //same kind// while every cell reads true. `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/failure-states/table-hides-a-plane`
* ''Minting Over a Retirement'' — a word seated beside one the graph already ruled, walking past the residue that says so. Greppable: `retires-to`. `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/failure-states/minting-over-a-retirement`
* ''Not Walking Before Minting'' — a finding derived at cost that the graph already held. A RETRIEVAL failure, never a knowledge one. `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/failure-states/not-walking-before-minting`
* ''Structure-Shaped Convention'' — a mechanism whose guarantee rides a register its substrate cannot enforce, so it reads structural and holds only by agreement. Greppable: name the enforcer, then ask who can seize it. `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/failure-states/structure-shaped-convention`
* ''The Empty Subject'' — a check that RAN, measured NOTHING, and reported SUCCESS: a gate pointed at an empty set, an absent subject, or a condition that cannot arise, returning the cleanest run it has ever produced. Greppable: run the matcher against the real corpus and read the count. `lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/failure-states/the-empty-subject`

<<~/ahu>>

